<Base title="Projects" description="Anywhim, Whimtrade, and what Giacomo Mari is building now.">
  <h1>Projects</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    Four things I have built, in the order they happened. Two of them no longer exist,
    which turns out to be the more useful half of the list.
  </p>

  <h2>Anywhim</h2>
  <span class="label">Retail company · 2021–2024 · Mantova, Italy</span>
  <p>
    A multi-site retail business in high-end fashion and resale, co-founded with two partners
    when I was 18. Over three years it grew to four stores — Mantova, Riccione, Cortina
    d’Ampezzo and Milano Marittima — a central warehouse, an online shop, and a wholesale
    brand, reaching €1,000,000 in annual turnover. At peak we were eight people and I was
    responsible for the team.
  </p>
  <p>
    It closed in December 2024. I have written more about why elsewhere, but the short version
    is that a business can be profitable at the till and still be the wrong shape underneath.
    I learned more from the wind-down than from any of the growth.
  </p>

